<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rodolfo Graziani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1882">1882</a>–<a href="/years/1955">1955</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rodolfo Graziani was an Italian general who directed the brutal reconquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, deporting the nomads of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a>. He commanded on the southern front in the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and became viceroy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-east-africa">Italian East Africa</a>, where an attempt on his life in 1937 was followed by mass killings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rodolfo-graziani.jpg" alt="Rodolfo Graziani" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marshal_Rodolfo_Graziani_potrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Nevertheless, Italian imperialism remains deeply contested, marked by the internment of much of Cyrenaica's population in camps and the execution of the resistance leader Omar Mukhtar in 1931, and by the massacre in Addis Ababa that followed the attempt on Viceroy <b>Rodolfo Graziani</b>'s life in February 1937.</blockquote><a href="/empire/italian-empire">Italian Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Italian rule was harsh: after an attempt on Viceroy <b>Rodolfo Graziani's</b> life in February 1937, thousands were massacred in Addis Ababa, and the monastery of Debre Libanos was attacked.</blockquote><a href="/state/italian-east-africa">Italian East Africa</a></li><li><blockquote>In Cyrenaica, <b>Rodolfo Graziani</b> deported much of the nomadic population into concentration camps where tens of thousands died, and Omar al-Mukhtar was hanged in 1931.</blockquote><a href="/state/italian-libya">Italian Libya</a></li></ul></section>
